# Sequence number wrapping with retransmission
# Client: 10.0.0.1:6000 -> Server: 10.0.0.2:80
# ISN_client=4294967200 (0xFFFFFFA0, near 2^32), ISN_server=500000
# Client sends 200 bytes total (100 + 100), wrapping past 2^32
# First 100-byte segment is retransmitted after nxt has wrapped
# Server sends 50 bytes
#
# ts_ms  src               dst               flags seq          ack     win    payload
0        10.0.0.1:6000     10.0.0.2:80       S     4294967200   0       65535  0
50       10.0.0.2:80       10.0.0.1:6000     SA    500000       4294967201 32768 0
55       10.0.0.1:6000     10.0.0.2:80       A     4294967201   500001  65535  0
# Client sends 100 bytes at seq 4294967201 -> wraps to nxt=5
100      10.0.0.1:6000     10.0.0.2:80       PA    4294967201   500001  65535  100
# Client sends another 100 bytes at seq 5 (past wrap) -> nxt=105
110      10.0.0.1:6000     10.0.0.2:80       PA    5            500001  65535  100
# Retransmission of first segment (seq 4294967201) while nxt=105
120      10.0.0.1:6000     10.0.0.2:80       PA    4294967201   500001  65535  100
# ACK covers both segments
150      10.0.0.2:80       10.0.0.1:6000     A     500001       105     32768  0
# Server sends 50 bytes
200      10.0.0.2:80       10.0.0.1:6000     PA    500001       105     32768  50
250      10.0.0.1:6000     10.0.0.2:80       A     105          500051  65535  0
# Clean close
300      10.0.0.1:6000     10.0.0.2:80       FA    105          500051  65535  0
350      10.0.0.2:80       10.0.0.1:6000     A     500051       106     32768  0
400      10.0.0.2:80       10.0.0.1:6000     FA    500051       106     32768  0
450      10.0.0.1:6000     10.0.0.2:80       A     106          500052  65535  0
